<%#
  THE WIRING TABLE'S COMPOSER, on its own (2026-11-02, the UX audit's B3/C4) so a refused connection
  comes back through Projects::ComposerRefusal as this partial again — open, with the error inside it
  and what was typed in each field. The maker's page draws it in the panel's head; the public page
  renders projects/_wiring with `editable: false` and never reaches it.

  Locals: project. Optional (a refusal): draft (the refused Maker::Connection), error, open.

  scope: :connection -- this form has no model object, so scope: is what names the params at all;
  Projects::ConnectionsController#create requires :connection, which scope: here produces (CLAUDE.md
  §14d's form-scope rule). Every field states its value, so none falls back to an @connection ivar.

  `submit->wiring#save` IS NOT DECORATION: this form sits inside the table's wiring controller, so
  its submit would otherwise just switch the leave-guard off, and an Add — which reloads the table —
  would drop every other row's unsaved edit without a word. With the action, wiring_controller.js
  asks first; the form is in no row, so every edited row counts.
%>
<% draft = local_assigns[:draft] %>
<% error = local_assigns[:error] %>
<details class="composer wiring-add" id="wiring-composer" <%= "open" if local_assigns[:open] %>>
  <summary class="btn small" aria-label="Add a connection">Add…</summary>
  <%= form_with url: project_connections_path(project), scope: :connection, class: "wiring-add-form",
                data: { action: "submit->wiring#save" } do |f| %>
    <% if error.present? %><div class="form-errors flash-alert composer-error" role="alert"><%= error %></div><% end %>
    <div class="composer-fields">
      <label class="field">
        <span>From</span>
        <%= f.text_field :from_label, value: draft&.from_label, placeholder: "e.g. Driver board", required: true %>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>To</span>
        <%= f.text_field :to_label, value: draft&.to_label, placeholder: "e.g. Stepper motor", required: true %>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Wire</span>
        <%= f.text_field :wire, value: draft&.wire, placeholder: "e.g. 22 AWG, pin 3" %>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Note</span>
        <%= f.text_field :note, value: draft&.note %>
      </label>
    </div>
    <%= f.submit "Add connection", class: "btn small" %>
  <% end %>
</details>
